    "message": "Here are revenue and order-line counts by region. Orders whose customer has no known region are grouped under null: 16 orders, 1,193.30 in revenue and 35 order lines.\n\nTo get these, I joined each order to its customer and then to the customer's region. Revenue is the sum of the order amounts. I counted order lines for each order first, then added those counts up by region. Doing it this way stops orders with several lines from having their amount added more than once. Order lines whose order isn't in the orders table aren't counted."
